  title: 'Indian Convicts and Migrants Mid-19th Century '
  info: 'The British brought Indian convicts to Singapore to construct roads, bridges,
    and buildings. Free Indian migrants followed, contributing to commerce, education,
    and religion. Their influence remains visible in Little India, a cultural enclave
    showcasing vibrant festivals like Deepavali and Thaipusam.  '
